{
 "doc": "Hiyuki Alt, colourway 02 / skin 1 (_port/rtx/skin1/Hiyuki2.pmx, written by _port/rtx/make_skin1_pmx.py: Hiyuki.pmx with every material renamed <name>2 and pointed at RGB copies of the 02 sheets in skin1/tex, matching the <name>2 VMTs of hiyuki_alt.mdl's second skin family; RGB because the game's alpha is a toon mask and the VMTs alpha-test at 0.5: read from the raw sheets, the published albedo cut skin 1 away in game, 2026-10-27). Same preset as hiyuki_08f3c33e (aggressive, satin gold 0.30 with f0 0.74, the game's normal maps at 1.0, body skin left to Remix); see its doc for the method. Differences in this colourway, from the game's FTM type mask: Kimono, ObiRibbon, Cuff and Headband are pale blue fabric (type 0/56, no metal), so Cuff and Headband are cloth here; the gold anklets, heel plates and black shoes of 01 are glossy pale blue (type 192) and become leather (glossy dielectric); the bow is cream fabric (hue 45-60), so the gold rule stops at hue 44 (recall 68%/57% of the game's gold on Up02/Down02 at 78%/50% precision; hue 25-60 took the bow: 55% precision); the sapphires stay blue and are taken by colour inside the gem rectangles measured on 01 (the obi's top gem turns grey here and stays cloth); nails are blue; Cloth02 has no gold in the game's mask, so it has no gold rule. Painted gold F0 (median linear luminance on the mesh): Up02 0.30, Down02 0.37, so f0 0.74 lifts it x2.5 and x2.0.",
